{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.84,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": [
        "R8"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "R8.1",
        "R8.2",
        "U1.7"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "+3V3",
        "Net-(U1-B)"
      ],
      "observed": "R8 is specified as 2.2 MΩ and is connected between +3V3 and the MAX3485 B pin (Net-(U1-B)). The SPICE deck also models it as 2.2 Meg.",
      "expected": "The design specification states R8 should be 2.2 kΩ as part of the MAX3485 A/B bias/fail-safe network. The R8 LCSC field C4190 is also consistent with the 2.2 kΩ value used for R15.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R6, R7, R8, R15 | 2k, 20k, 2.2k, 2.2k"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R8\") (value \"2.2M\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"40\") (name \"Net-(U1-B)\") (node (ref \"R15\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"B\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R8 +3V3 Net-_U1-B_ 2.2Meg"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This changes the B-line bias from an intended 2.2 kΩ/2.2 kΩ divider to an effectively 2.2 kΩ pull-down with only a very weak 2.2 MΩ pull-up, pulling U1 B close to ground. That alters the MAX3485 differential idle/fail-safe state and receiver switching threshold, which can make serial-mode half-duplex servo communication unreliable or different from the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist and SPICE deck agree on a R8 value of 2.2 MΩ, while the specification and the component's LCSC field indicate the intended R8 value is 2.2 kΩ. This is a clear deviation in the MAX3485 bias network and is the main anomaly."
}

